cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these bounds, data or verifiers, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "Certified bounds for the Mertens function: lim sup M(x)/sqrt(x) > 1.92036 and lim inf M(x)/sqrt(x) < -1.92053"
authors:
  - family-names: Weisz
    given-names: Benjamin
repository-code: "https://github.com/wbeni95/mertens-function-bounds"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
keywords:
  - Mertens function
  - Mertens conjecture
  - Riemann zeta function
  - certified computation
  - ball arithmetic
abstract: >-
  A self-contained, independently checkable proof that lim sup M(x)/sqrt(x) > 1.9203693129093421 and
  lim inf M(x)/sqrt(x) < -1.9205369736317600, improving the bounds of Hurst (2018) on both sides. Ingham's theorem is
  applied at two explicit points; the finite sum over the first 14 400 zeta zeros is evaluated in ball arithmetic.
  Includes two verifiers based on different software, the zero data, and timestamped evidence of a timed run.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Hurst
        given-names: Greg
    title: "Computations of the Mertens function and improved bounds on the Mertens conjecture"
    journal: "Mathematics of Computation"
    volume: 87
    issue: 310
    start: 1013
    end: 1028
    year: 2018
    doi: "10.1090/mcom/3275"
